WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.440
 Some people would think this the last name of the ever-made that we've been

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.000
 first.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.500
 And I have two young men who are so well behaved sitting there waiting for

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.000
 grammar.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.000
 So I think it's time we end up more than alive.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.000
 I'd like to thank you, Sondarshan.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.000
 I'm glad you're here.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:26.900
 Welcome,

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:33.900
 and I'm glad you're here.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:38.900
 I'm glad you're here.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:44.900
 I'm glad you're here.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:59.900
 I'm glad you're here.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:05.900
 Namaste and good evening.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:13.900
 In India, the word "bibi" literally means an elder sister.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:18.900
 But metaphorically, the word means much more.

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:24.900
 It signifies a go-to person for the younger siblings,

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:30.900
 someone who has a cool head and a lot of knowledge and some judgment.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:37.900
 In other words, a "bibi" has answers to life's questions.

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:46.900
 Every lucky family has one, and every immigrant community is surely fortunate

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:48.900
 to have one.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:59.900
 Our Indian community's "bibi" is called Mona Ala.

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:08.210
 For Mona, the involvement in social causes began at a very young age when a

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:11.900
 woman friend in distress asked for help.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:15.900
 Then another one asked, and then another.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:23.330
 That led eventually to the creation of Association of Asian Indian Women of

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:23.900
 Ohio,

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:26.900
 a support group for women in distress.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:31.900
 Mona has been there at the inception of Project SEVA.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:34.900
 The word "SEVA" means selfless service.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:41.920
 SEVA has provided meals, blankets, hygiene packets to countless individuals

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:44.900
 throughout Northeast Ohio.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:49.900
 Mona has made a single contribution to the Indian Cultural Guard,

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:56.830
 where the statue of Mahatma Gandhi stands proudly on Martin Luther King Jr.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:57.900
 Boulevard.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:04.370
 And of course, Mona has been an integral part of FICA, the umbrella

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:09.900
 organization of Asian Indians in Northeast Ohio.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:16.560
 In other words, there is no effort undertaken by the Indian community in the

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.900
 cultural, philanthropic,

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:25.900
 or the service realm that Mona has been a significant part of.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:29.900
 Mona, your FICA family is proud of you.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:35.900
 The larger Indian community is proud of you for being chosen for this honor.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:43.270
 And I think Dr. Mohan Bhapna, the immediate past recipient of the very same

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:47.900
 award, said it best, very said.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:50.580
 And I quote, "There is no more deserving person for this honor than Mrs. Mona

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:54.900
 Mahatma.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:04:00.900
 She is a diligent and humble pillar of the Indian community. Congratulations."

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:22.180
 And today it is my high honor to induct you in the Pumice International College

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:23.900
 Award.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:55.900
 Thank you for your attention. I truly appreciate your kind words.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:05:01.930
 If I could break your indulgence just for a moment, a shout out to my grandson's

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:02.900
 hearing.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:06.900
 My two dates for the evening, I got lucky, I got two dates.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.900
 Our 9-year-old saturn and 5-year-old

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:17.900
 her.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:23.900
 And of course, the other undergraduates in California, Samay and I have.

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:26.900
 I call them my heart and soul.

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:32.900
 And the 5-year-old wanted to know what his place was on the phone call.

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:36.900
 So he said, "What is more important, honey, the heart or the soul?"

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:41.900
 And I said, "That's a bit complicated. I'll give back to you."

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:47.110
 And we looked straight at the eyes and he said, "You should not say complicated

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:47.900
 things."

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:54.900
 That's not a life lesson, I don't know what it is.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:06:05.100
 When your efforts are noticed and acknowledged, it gives you an impetus to not

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:07.900
 only continue what you're doing,

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:11.900
 but to put a little more effort into it.

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:19.900
 And then to be surrounded by such dignitaries where in front of them my resume

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.900
 is just a footnote.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:31.030
 I am so honored to be in your presence and to be counted in the same group as

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:32.900
 you are.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:36.900
 Where we come from in India, it is not...

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:43.900
 First of all, my experiences are not global, national or even statewide.

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:51.900
 My efforts and interests and pursuits have been just local, Cleveland.

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:55.900
 And that too, a very small part of Cleveland, the Indian community.

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:59.900
 My focus has just been in the Indian community.

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:08.300
 And mainly both of women, young mothers and daughters, who for some reason or

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:12.900
 the other have fallen on difficult times.

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:19.220
 Where we come from in our culture, we don't talk about your problems, it's

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:19.900
 taboo.

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:24.900
 I speak of rural India now, you are not urban.

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:31.570
 And when you realize that that mindset of rural India has found its way to the

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:32.900
 United States,

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:34.900
 it's very troubling.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:40.900
 And you see these young girls and women, mothers who are here,

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:46.900
 experiencing some of the same issues that they did back home.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:52.530
 It talks about your heartstrings and you want to make things a little bit

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:53.900
 better for them.

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:58.900
 Maybe one day they will all be able to rise up and say,

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:04.900
 "It is not my fault that this thing is not working, my marriage is not working."

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:09.900
 Or something is going wrong in my life, it is not just my fault.

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:12.900
 To give you a small example,

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:19.320
 I got a call from an acquaintance of mine, who had literally a phone number and

00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:19.900
 said,

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:25.900
 "Would you please talk to this young lady, she doesn't feel safe at all."

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:32.900
 I spoke with her and I found out the reason she didn't feel safe was because

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:34.900
 she had three daughters

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:39.900
 and wasn't able to give her family a son.

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:44.350
 And she felt that there was something going on and she didn't feel safe for her

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:46.900
 daughters or for herself.

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:51.900
 And she just needed a place to hide for a week.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:54.900
 Then she said the storm grew over.

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:58.900
 I never thought anything of it.

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:07.450
 I got in my car, what I came to mind was a hymn from our Holy Scriptures which

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:09.900
 says, translated, says,

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:15.510
 "God gave me the strength and the wisdom in order to shy away from something

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:16.900
 that is right."

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:23.900
 I got in my car and I brought her home, the three kids and the mother.

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:29.300
 And much to the order of my husband, we saw our own two kids and three little

00:09:29.300 --> 00:09:29.900
 girls

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:33.900
 under the age of seven running around in the house.

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:39.620
 And when I explained to him what it was, the good, decent human being that he

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:39.900
 is,

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:44.900
 all he said was, "Be careful, don't get into any trouble."

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:49.900
 A week later I found out that the husband was truly repentant

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:54.900
 and he wanted his wife and his children home.

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:57.900
 There was no mention of son or daughter.

00:09:57.900 --> 00:10:00.900
 He just wanted his children home.

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:08.200
 And I realized that such a small effort in my heart changed the path of their

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:08.900
 lives.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:16.900
 And now two of these young girls are in medicine and one of them is a lawyer.

00:10:16.900 --> 00:10:23.900
 So how do you... how do you not reach out to them?

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:30.900
 How do you not put an extra effort to make a difference in their lives?

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:39.900
 A few years ago, a couple of friends and myself, Dr. Jaya Shah and Dr. Hiba Gokwani,

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:44.900
 we formed a very informal sort of group called Helping Hands.

00:10:44.900 --> 00:10:51.900
 And what Helping Hands does is it provides anything from a ride to the hospital,

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:56.900
 a home cooked meal when a spouse is unwary,

00:10:56.900 --> 00:11:03.900
 a little bit of lighthouse work if needed, somebody's sick, they can't do it.

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:13.900
 I believe we have gotten hundreds and hundreds of calls towards that end.

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:21.900
 One thing that would stay with me until the day I died was a young couple

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:30.230
 had moved to Cleveland just for a few months because his mother was on her last

00:11:30.230 --> 00:11:30.900
 days.

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:36.900
 And she was so weak she couldn't sit up and read from the Holy Scriptures,

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:40.900
 the same faith that she was from the same faith that I am.

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:46.200
 So the daughter of Gokwani said, "Would you be able to come and read the

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:48.900
 morning prayers for her?"

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:52.900
 Because she has not gone without that person today.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:55.900
 It's a long prayer, it's about an hour and a half.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:58.900
 But I said, "Okay, I will do it."

00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:03.900
 Every day I would go there. For seven to eight days I went,

00:12:03.900 --> 00:12:07.900
 and every day I went, she would... when she said, "Bye," she would say,

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:12.900
 "See you tomorrow." And I went the next day.

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:18.900
 Till on the eight days she sort of, you know, "Okay, that's enough."

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:23.900
 And on the ninth day she died.

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:31.900
 The look in her eyes, the gratitude would always stay with me.

00:12:31.900 --> 00:12:39.900
 So these are the kind of things we like to do to make life a little easier,

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:45.900
 a little more bearable for someone who has all of them at hard times.

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:50.900
 So be it the Federation of India Community Association, the Project SEGA,

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:58.410
 or the Association of Asian Indian Women, with its helpline, which still exists

00:12:58.410 --> 00:12:58.900
 today,

00:12:58.900 --> 00:13:05.900
 or helping hands. Wherever there is a need, we are a host of volunteers

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:10.900
 who will always, always come through for you.

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:15.900
 So if anyone of you knows of any family or an individual

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:20.900
 that has fallen on difficult times, please get...

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:26.900
 contact that handsome and he will in turn get the message to me.

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:28.900
 Thank you very much.

